  data: {
    LLM: "1. Players place wagers on Player, Banker, or Tie. 2. Dealer deals two cards to Player and two to Banker. 3. If either has 8 or 9 (natural), both stand and hands are compared. 4. Otherwise: Player draws on 0-5, stands on 6-7. 5. Banker follows fixed Third Card Matrix based on Player's third card (if any). 6. Compare final totals; closest to 9 wins. Tie returns all wagers. Banker wins: 1:1 minus 5% commission.",
    Player: "1. Players place wagers on Player, Banker, or Tie. 2. Dealer deals two cards to Player and two to Banker. 3. If either has 8 or 9 (natural), both stand and hands are compared. 4. Otherwise: Player draws on 0-5, stands on 6-7. 5. Banker follows fixed Third Card Matrix based on Player's third card (if any). 6. Compare final totals; closest to 9 wins. Tie returns all wagers. Banker wins: 1:1 minus 5% commission.",
    objective: 'Predict which of the two hands (Player or Banker) will have a total closest to 9.',
    gameplay: "1. Players place wagers on Player, Banker, or Tie. 2. Dealer deals two cards to Player and two to Banker. 3. If either has 8 or 9 (natural), both stand and hands are compared. 4. Otherwise: Player draws on 0-5, stands on 6-7. 5. Banker follows fixed Third Card Matrix based on Player's third card (if any). 6. Compare final totals; closest to 9 wins. Tie returns all wagers. Banker wins: 1:1 minus 5% commission.",
    keyRules: [
      'The Banker bet wins slightly more often than the Player bet.',
      'Tie bets pay 8:1 (or 9:1 in some venues).',
      'Winning Banker bets are subject to a 5% commission payable to the house.',
